  "guard": "A statement about what the native 4v4 action interface can express relative to the scaffold's injected defender behavior on the sealed A' episodes. HIGH_COVERAGE_REPRESENTABLE_NATIVE means the episode-clustered LCB95 of the pass rate reached the pre-declared 0.90 on every gate and pole using a GO_TO-only, greedy, future-seeing path-oracle; it is constructive evidence of high-coverage representability, NOT a claim that the interface reproduces DEFEND at every state. A NOT_REPRESENTABLE_* label means the frozen coverage was not reached by that greedy oracle, not that no action sequence exists. Representability is not learnability, not a win-rate claim, and not evidence about pi_B or 6v6.",
  "claim_boundary": "A statement about what the native 4v4 action interface can express relative to the scaffold's injected defender behavior on the sealed A' episodes, at the pre-declared 0.90 coverage and using a GO_TO-only greedy path-oracle. 'High-coverage representability' is not 'the interface reproduces DEFEND everywhere', and a NOT_REPRESENTABLE label is not a proof of impossibility. It is not a statement about whether PPO would learn that behavior, not a win-rate claim, and not evidence about pi_B or 6v6.",
